Elevator (hello interview version)

Same structure as ../elevator (strategies, observers, door, panels, displays).
The difference is how stops are stored and when the elevator stops.


Request

- Request(floor, type)
- PICKUP_UP     hall call, passenger wants to go up
- PICKUP_DOWN   hall call, passenger wants to go down
- DESTINATION   button inside the cabin, stop no matter the direction
- HallPanel.callLift(direction)  -> Request.pickup(floor, direction) -> controller.requestElevator
- ElevatorPanel.pressFloor(floor) -> Request.destination(floor) -> elevator.addRequest

The elevator keeps one Set<Request> instead of upStops / downStops.
A Set also ignores duplicate presses of the same button.


Direction-aware stopping

- Going up, the elevator stops for PICKUP_UP and DESTINATION only.
- Going down, it stops for PICKUP_DOWN and DESTINATION only.
- A PICKUP_DOWN above an elevator going up is skipped. It is served after the elevator turns around.
- When nothing matching is left ahead, it rides to the furthest opposite pickup and turns there.
- On arrival, only the requests that match the new direction are removed.


Swappable logic

- ElevatorAssignmentStrategy picks the elevator for a hall call.
  CommittedIdleNearestAssignment is the hello interview one:
    1. elevator moving the requested way, not past the floor, with a stop at or beyond it
    2. else nearest idle elevator
    3. else nearest elevator
- ElevatorMovementStrategy picks the next stop. LookMovementStrategy sweeps in one direction,
  then reverses (SCAN / LOOK).
